SUMMARY:UTM v5.0.7
DESCRIPTION:UTM 5.0.7 | Universal IPA\n\n## Highlights\n* (macOS) **DirectX
  graphics support for Windows**: Modern accelerated graphics for Windows 1
 1 is now available on UTM for the first time. The driver is still experime
 ntal and games compatibility is currently limited.\n* **Vulkan 1.3 graphic
 s support for Linux**: Vulkan 1.3 is now supported on Linux guests with Vi
 rtIO Venus drivers in Mesa. Additionally\, OpenGL 4.1 is supported with th
 e new Apple Core OpenGL backend (macOS only).\n* **Snapshots**: Save your 
 VM at any point and go back to it later from the new Snapshots tab. Works 
 with QEMU VMs on macOS and iOS 26\, and with Apple Virtualization VMs on m
 acOS 27.\n* (macOS) **Apple Virtualization on macOS 27**: Pass USB devices
  through to your VM\, turn on Secure Boot for Linux\, run a VM without sav
 ing changes\, and let VMs talk to each other with new networking modes.\n*
  (iOS) **Better touch controls**: Gestures respond immediately\, with new 
 middle-click and right-drag actions and a new drag-to-scroll touch mode.\n
 * (iOS) **iPhone Duo**: Fold your iPhone Duo like a laptop\, and the botto
 m half becomes a keyboard or touchpad for your VM.\n\n## Notes\n* Suspende
 d VMs may not resume correctly after updating. We recommend shutting down 
 all VMs before you update UTM.\n* The minimum supported versions are now m
 acOS 12 and iOS 15.\n* We now have a [development blog](https://blog.getut
 m.app)! Follow us for in-depth technical deep dives such as how we brought
  DirectX to QEMU.\n* (macOS) To use the new graphics driver for Windows 11
 \, we recommend a fresh install because the driver is still experimental a
 nd its use could lead to instability in the system. During the install of 
 the guest tools\, you will be prompted to select the experimental graphics
  driver. If you wish to install the new driver on a system that already is
  running the older display only driver\, you need to run the uninstall scr
 ipt provided on the guest tools install ISO first.\n* (macOS) Apple CoreGL
  backend does not support Vulkan or Di
URL:https://raynmahbub.github.io/OmniSource/feeds/utm.json
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:streamyfin-0.55.2@omnisource
DTSTAMP:20261016T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
SUMMARY:Streamyfin v0.55.2
DESCRIPTION:Streamyfin 0.55.2 | streamyfin-ios\n\n## What's Changed\n\n0.55
 .2 is another bug fix release. One thing does change: a TV is now signed i
 n from your phone with Quick Connect\, so Quick Connect has to be on in yo
 ur server's dashboard (it is by default) and both devices need this versio
 n. The rest again comes out of the crash and error reports\, plus a round 
 of fixes to accounts and the Seerr sign-in\n\nThanks to everyone who repor
 ted a problem\, and to @Gauvino for the Quick Connect and Seerr fixes!\n\n
 ### ✨ Highlights\n- **Signing a TV in from your phone uses Quick Connect
 **\, with a code or a QR code\, and no longer sends your password over the
  local network (#2240) by @Gauvino\n- **Freezes of a few seconds when play
 back starts or resumes** on iOS and tvOS are fixed (#2205) by @fredrikburm
 ester\n- **Access tokens are kept out of the app log**\, including the log
 s you export\, and entries written by earlier versions are cleaned up (#21
 03) by @Gauvino\n- **Seerr access no longer carries over** to the next acc
 ount signed in on the same device (#2233) by @Gauvino\n- **Quick Connect i
 n Settings** sends the code on its sixth digit and tells you why a code fa
 ils (#2246) by @Gauvino\n- **Luxembourgish** is available as an app langua
 ge (#2195) by @Gauvino\n\n### 🎬 Player\n- iOS and tvOS: the app no long
 er freezes for several seconds when playback starts or resumes while the s
 ystem audio service is slow to answer (#2205) by @fredrikburmester\n- Musi
 c: tapping a track far down the queue before the rest has loaded no longer
  fails\, and neither do previous and next with repeat all (#2212) by @fred
 rikburmester\n\n### 📺 TV\n- Pairing a TV with a phone goes through Quic
 k Connect: the TV shows a code and a QR code\, your phone approves it\, an
 d the TV signs in by itself. No password travels between the two devices\,
  and the TV picks its own server (#2240) by @Gauvino\n- On the phone\, Set
 tings > Log in on TV scans the QR code or takes the code typed in\, and th
 e entry now shows on iPhones too (#2240) by @Gauvino\n- T
URL:https://raynmahbub.github.io/OmniSource/feeds/streamyfin.json
END:VEVENT
